>>> following toy example.
>>>
>>> Suppose I have many store receipts:
>>>
>>> receipt1 <- (item = c(shirt, pants, socks), price = c(20, 30, 5))
>>>
>>> receipt2 <- (item = c(socks, shoes), price = c(5, 80))
>>>
>>> receipt3 <- (item = c(shirt, pants, socks, shoes), price = c(20, 30, 5,
>>> 80))
>>>
>>> receipt4 <- (item = c(shirt, pants, socks, shoes, belt, hat), price =
>>> c(20, 30, 5, 80, 20, 25))
>>>
>>>
>>>
>>> where receiptN consists of a varying number of items (in practice a LARGE
>>> factor w/ ~10k levels) and corresponding prices.
>>>
>>> given that tidy data puts observations in rows - and it would seem here
>>> that the logical unit of observation is receipt - how should one the
>>> resulting table be arranged?
